What is the principal amount which earns Rs. 154 as compound interest for the second year at 10% per annum?
Rs. 1540
Rs. 1340
Rs. 1200
Rs. 1400
Solution:

The compound interest for the second year equals 10% of the amount at the end of the first year.

Let the principal be P.

Amount after year 1 = P × 1.1
Interest for year 2 = 10% of 1.1P = 0.11P

Setting this equal to 154:

0.11P = 154

P = 154 / 0.11 = 1400
Option:D
